meta {
  name: Get Product Attribute by ID
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.type: eq TextAttribute
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/product-attributes/{id}` -- fetch a single product attribute by
  its Mongo ObjectId.

  Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Fetches the kept `TextAttribute` fixture from
  "Create Product Attribute.bru".

  ## _fields is ignored on GET-by-id (new finding this session)
  `GET /product-attributes/{id}?_fields=id&_fields=group_ids` still returns the
  **full** shape (`id, name, label, description, status, created, modified,
  account_id, type, character_limit`), ignoring the `_fields` restriction
  entirely. **`_fields` only applies to list/search endpoints, never to
  single-resource `GET /{resource}/{id}`.** Generalizes Phase 0's `_fields`
  findings.

  ## Subpath discovery
  `GET .../bogus_xyz` -- 400, raw field list:
  `['id','account_id','name','label','description','status','group_ids',
  'product_family_ids','created','modified','character_limit','type']`.
  Includes `group_ids` and an undocumented `product_family_ids` (not in the
  spec's `ProductAttributeGetOutputDto`) -- neither actually appears in a full
  `GET` response body though (see `group_ids` linkage question in the POST file).

  ## WARNING: GET /product-attributes listing leaks cross-tenant data
  The **list** endpoint (`GET /product-attributes`) returns attributes from
  other accounts -- a confirmed data-isolation bug. Use `GET /{id}` exclusively
  until Plytix resolves this.
}

example {
  name: 200 - Success (BooleanAttribute)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-21. Full shape for a BooleanAttribute from the pre-existing account fixtures.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes/6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cc
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cc",
            "name": "Includes Zipper",
            "label": "zippered",
            "description": null,
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "created": "2026-06-22T08:45:07.391000",
            "modified": "2026-06-22T08:45:07.391000",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "type": "BooleanAttribute"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
